jobs.description:
Are you looking for a job at a manufacturing company with varied responsibilities? This is a position as an operator working in a 5-shift rotation in the packaging department. In this role, you’ll work as a production worker in a 5-shift rotation at a company in Ittervoort. Your daily tasks will include:

- Operating the (packaging) machine and troubleshooting malfunctions during the packaging process;
- Operating the mixer, where raw materials are blended;
- Working in accordance with HACCP guidelines to ensure food safety;
- Restocking products using a forklift.

You will work in a 5-shift rotation, with the following schedules: 1:45 p.m. – 10:15 p.m., 9:45 p.m. – 6:15 a.m., 5:45 a.m. – 2:15 p.m. (8,5 hours per day).

You can work in various roles, including loader, mixer, filler, and packer. You’ll learn all of this on the job. 

- MBO-level work and thinking skills, preferably in the field of food or engineering. Do you happen to have experience in the food industry? Then you have an edge!;
- Experience operating machinery;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English for safety regulations;
- You have an eye for detail, and you’re also flexible and able to handle stress.

Do you have a forklift certification? That’s a definite plus!

Work in a international production team and help make high-quality products. You'll operate machines, check quality, and keep everything running smoothly. As a Production Employee, your tasks are broad and varied. While some tasks are repetitive, employees rotate weekly between different workstations and responsibilities. This ensures that you remain widely deployable, engaged, and continuously developing new skills.

What you'll do:

- Operating and monitoring production machines;
- Performing quality checks and completing required documentation;
- Counting, stamping, and registering production time;
- Preparing finished products and orders for shipping;
- Keeping your workspace clean, organized, and safe;
- Reporting deviations, malfunctions, or quality issues to your team leader.

You will work in three shifts:

- 06:00 – 14:00
- 14:00 – 22:00
- 22:00 – 06:00

- Good knowledge of the English language;
- Ability to work accurately and precisely – this is the most important requirement;
- Basic computer skills (data entry, forms, registrations);
- A focused mindset with the ability to work quickly and efficiently;
- Flexibility and willingness to learn and rotate between workstations;
- Availability and motivation to work in a 3- as well as a 2-shift system;
